            <ArticleTitle>Acute and chronic hypertensive headache and hypertensive encephalopathy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>313-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Three patients are described who experienced headache from hypertension: one had acute headache from acute hypertension, one had daily, morning headaches from chronic hypertension, and one had acute headache with generalized tonic-clonic seizure from hypertensive encephalopathy. The presumed pathophysiological mechanisms involved in the three hypertensive headache conditions are reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
